KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
must never appear
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/11: a non-virtual constructor of a class template shall not
be implicitly instantiated unless odr-used.  The two-argument constructor here
is never used, so under full lazy instantiation its assertion "must never
appear" should not enter the goto program.

CBMC still instantiates constructors eagerly: deferring the special members
(constructors/destructors) along with ordinary members and operators was
attempted but destabilised container verification (e.g. std::vector / std::map
runs diverged in BMC even though the goto program had fewer functions),
pointing at a needed special member being instantiated with a divergent body
under the lazy path.  Pending that investigation the forbidden message still
appears, so this is KNOWNBUG.  Tracks the remaining [temp.inst]/11 work; see
doc/architectural/cpp-extern-template-member-instantiation.md §13.
